Dialogue: 2,0:00:00.20,0:01:16.34,Hook,,0,0,0,,{\an8\pos(540,54)\fad(200,0)\fnRoundHog SemiBold\fs34\c&H00B3DA43}Matt Lenhard (Vectoral)
Dialogue: 2,0:00:00.20,0:01:16.34,Hook,,0,0,0,,{\an8\pos(540,118)\fad(200,0)}“One attack: 100,000
Dialogue: 2,0:00:00.20,0:01:16.34,Hook,,0,0,0,,{\an8\pos(540,190)\fad(200,0)}requests from 4,000 accounts
Dialogue: 2,0:00:00.20,0:01:16.34,Hook,,0,0,0,,{\an8\pos(540,262)\fad(200,0)}in 100 milliseconds”
Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.10,0:00:01.94,Caption,,0,0,0,,So for context
Dialogue: 0,0:00:01.94,0:00:04.40,Caption,,0,0,0,,we stop like inference
Dialogue: 0,0:00:04.40,0:00:06.18,Caption,,0,0,0,,abuse and like token
Dialogue: 0,0:00:06.18,0:00:07.10,Caption,,0,0,0,,fraud. So everything
Dialogue: 0,0:00:07.10,0:00:08.60,Caption,,0,0,0,,from like CSAM
Dialogue: 0,0:00:08.60,0:00:09.85,Caption,,0,0,0,,distillation
Dialogue: 0,0:00:09.94,0:00:10.78,Caption,,0,0,0,,cyber attacks being
Dialogue: 0,0:00:10.78,0:00:13.46,Caption,,0,0,0,,proxied through AI
Dialogue: 0,0:00:13.46,0:00:14.21,Caption,,0,0,0,,endpoints.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:14.21,0:00:15.69,Caption,,0,0,0,,So we recently saw an
Dialogue: 0,0:00:15.69,0:00:17.53,Caption,,0,0,0,,attack that was across
Dialogue: 0,0:00:17.53,0:00:19.25,Caption,,0,0,0,,probably 3,000
Dialogue: 0,0:00:19.25,0:00:21.50,Caption,,0,0,0,,4,000 accounts
Dialogue: 0,0:00:21.53,0:00:23.79,Caption,,0,0,0,,100,000 requests all
Dialogue: 0,0:00:23.79,0:00:26.45,Caption,,0,0,0,,within 100 milliseconds
Dialogue: 0,0:00:26.45,0:00:28.09,Caption,,0,0,0,,and this person had been
Dialogue: 0,0:00:28.09,0:00:28.61,Caption,,0,0,0,,sitting on these
Dialogue: 0,0:00:28.61,0:00:29.41,Caption,,0,0,0,,accounts for a while.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:29.41,0:00:31.03,Caption,,0,0,0,,Some were bought up from
Dialogue: 0,0:00:31.03,0:00:32.61,Caption,,0,0,0,,the underground markets
Dialogue: 0,0:00:32.61,0:00:33.47,Caption,,0,0,0,,some were probably spun
Dialogue: 0,0:00:33.47,0:00:34.49,Caption,,0,0,0,,up from automation.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:34.49,0:00:36.89,Caption,,0,0,0,,But it shows you...
Dialogue: 0,0:00:36.89,0:00:38.19,Caption,,0,0,0,,I guess with the power
Dialogue: 0,0:00:38.19,0:00:39.65,Caption,,0,0,0,,of AI, what's possible
Dialogue: 0,0:00:39.65,0:00:41.17,Caption,,0,0,0,,where an attack can now
Dialogue: 0,0:00:41.17,0:00:43.41,Caption,,0,0,0,,be, if they just want a
Dialogue: 0,0:00:43.41,0:00:44.27,Caption,,0,0,0,,few things to slip
Dialogue: 0,0:00:44.27,0:00:45.75,Caption,,0,0,0,,through, it might be a
Dialogue: 0,0:00:45.75,0:00:47.07,Caption,,0,0,0,,million requests across
Dialogue: 0,0:00:47.07,0:00:48.21,Caption,,0,0,0,,a large number of
Dialogue: 0,0:00:48.21,0:00:50.50,Caption,,0,0,0,,accounts all at once.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:50.61,0:00:52.74,Caption,,0,0,0,,We think of it really as
Dialogue: 0,0:00:52.83,0:00:54.57,Caption,,0,0,0,,anomaly detection.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:54.57,0:00:56.49,Caption,,0,0,0,,Can you, specifically in
Dialogue: 0,0:00:56.49,0:00:57.99,Caption,,0,0,0,,terms of endpoint
Dialogue: 0,0:00:57.99,0:00:58.75,Caption,,0,0,0,,security
Dialogue: 0,0:00:58.75,0:01:00.21,Caption,,0,0,0,,can you detect
Dialogue: 0,0:01:00.21,0:01:01.35,Caption,,0,0,0,,anomalies?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:01.37,0:01:03.75,Caption,,0,0,0,,across a large number of
Dialogue: 0,0:01:03.75,0:01:06.16,Caption,,0,0,0,,accounts extremely fast.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:06.16,0:01:07.08,Caption,,0,0,0,,It's a hard problem
Dialogue: 0,0:01:07.08,0:01:08.28,Caption,,0,0,0,,like how do you roll up
Dialogue: 0,0:01:08.28,0:01:09.76,Caption,,0,0,0,,if you've got 100,000
Dialogue: 0,0:01:09.76,0:01:10.70,Caption,,0,0,0,,requests coming in
Dialogue: 0,0:01:10.70,0:01:11.42,Caption,,0,0,0,,how do you roll up
Dialogue: 0,0:01:11.42,0:01:12.62,Caption,,0,0,0,,what's normal for those
Dialogue: 0,0:01:12.62,0:01:15.18,Caption,,0,0,0,,accounts all at once in
Dialogue: 0,0:01:15.18,0:01:16.34,Caption,,0,0,0,,milliseconds?
